          "similarity_score": 0.3113082,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## Dental procedures\n\n- D2391: tooth-coloured filling on one surface of a back tooth - $210\n- D2140: silver (amalgam) filling on one surface - $160\n- D7140: simple tooth extraction - $240",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2858,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.25243837,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## Medical procedures\n\n- 93000: resting 12-lead electrocardiogram, with the doctor's reading of it - $65\n- 94010: spirometry - $85\n- 93784: 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure monitoring - $140\n- 81002: urine dipstick test done in the clinic - $15\n- 69210: ear wax removal, per ear - $75\n- 17110: wart freezing (cryotherapy), up to 14 warts in one session - $90",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2858,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.2394892,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## A code you do not recognise\n\nIf your receipt shows a code that is not in this list, the front desk can tell you what it is.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2858,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.22493131,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n\nYour itemized receipt lists each procedure done at your visit by its billing code. Medical procedures use five-digit CPT codes, and dental procedures use CDT codes that start with the letter D. If you pay out of pocket, each procedure below is charged at the price shown, in addition to the rate for the visit at which it is done.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2857,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.15682957,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Medical examinations for work, driving and sport\n\nWe do not carry out commercial driver (DOT) medical examinations, pilot medicals or immigration medical examinations. A sports physical before joining a team or a competition is done in a standard GP appointment.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2851,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.15216598,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Preparing for tests at the clinic\n\nSome tests are done at the clinic during a regular appointment. This guide explains how to prepare for each of them. If your doctor has given you different instruc",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2851,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.14789104,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Preparing for tests at the clinic\n## Electrocardiogram (ECG)\n\nA resting 12-lead ECG records the electrical activity of your heart through ten small sticky electrodes placed on your chest, arms and l",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2849,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.1472022,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Blue Cross Blue Shield\n\nWe are in-network with Blue Cross Blue Shield PPO plans, including BlueCard PPO members whose plan was issued in another state; look for the suitcase ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2857,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.13703199,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Minor procedures\n\nWe freeze common warts and verrucas with cryotherapy (liquid nitrogen). A wart may need two to four treatments, about three weeks apart. We do not remo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2850,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.13087636,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Dental care guide\n## Before your appointment\n\nTell the dentist before any treatment if you take a blood-thinning medicine such as warfarin, apixaban (Eliquis) or clopidogrel (Plavix), or if you have",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2849,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.12613392,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n\nThis guide lists, plan by plan, the health insurance plans we are in-network with. Insurance companies sell many plans under one brand name, and being in-network with a company",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2855,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.123534575,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Language interpreters\n\nFree telephone interpreting is available in more than 200 languages for any appointment. Ask for it when you book or when you check in; there is",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2855,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.122789174,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Registering as a new patient\n\nNew patients fill in three forms at their first visit:\n\n- Form PR-1, New Patient Registration: your contact details, emergency contact an",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2850,
          "chunk_index": 5,
          "similarity_score": 0.12189981,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Dental care guide\n## After a tooth extraction\n\nBite firmly on the gauze pad for 30 to 45 minutes to let a blood clot form. Do not rinse your mouth for the first 24 hours; after that, rinse gently wi",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2854,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.12025362,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Messages we will never send\n\nWe will never ask for your card number, bank details, Social Security number or insurance member ID by text message",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2856,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.11855987,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n## Conversations with the chat assistant\n\nConversations with the clinic's chat assistant are kept with your appointment records. Clinic staff can read them, ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2854,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.11353828,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Text message reminders\n\nWe send a reminder by text message 48 hours before your appointment and another 2 hours before it. Our messages always c",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2852,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.11267092,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Tetanus, diphtheria and whooping cough (Tdap)\n\nAdults need a tetanus booster every 10 years. We use Boostrix, which also protects against diphtheria and whooping cough (pertussis).",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2850,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.11241573,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Dental care guide\n## Dental insurance\n\nMedical insurance plans do not cover dental care. For dental appointments we accept these dental plans: Delta Dental PPO, MetLife PDP Plus and Guardian DentalG",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2840,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.111644626,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do I need a referral from a primary care doctor to book with a specialist?\nAnswer: You can book a visit with any of our practitioners without a referral.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2841,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.111318946,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I bring to my first appointment?\nAnswer: Please bring a valid photo ID, your insurance card, and any relevant prior lab or test results related to your case.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2850,
          "chunk_index": 6,
          "similarity_score": 0.10920247,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Dental care guide\n## Services we do not offer\n\nWe do not offer teeth whitening, orthodontic treatment such as braces or clear aligners, or dental implants.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2853,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.10809648,
